just about an hour ago the ntsb  announced it is stepping in to help the  investigation into that deadly crash  joel mohler joining us now live from  north las vegas with what was discussed  and what is next joe  that's right the ntsb held that press  conference here at city hall just a few  hours ago to explain that they will be  conducting their own investigation this  is separate from what the police  department is doing they will be looking  into how speed play to factor into this  crash and to provide recommendations on  how to avoid these crashes from  happening again in the future we were  out there at the intersection where this  all happened when their crews arrived  while we were trying to piece together  how this all unfolded  the ntsb arrived to the intersection  monday morning to help north las vegas  police look into the crash that killed  nine people saturday afternoon many  people are now scratching their heads  wondering how this crash was so bad the  driver of this challenger was going  north here on commerce where the speed  limit is only 35 miles per hour  according to officials he got to this  red light at cheyenne and ran right  through it that challenger was going  over 100 miles per hour according to  police when it went through the  intersection hitting several vehicles  including a toyota sienna band with a  family of seven the impact here at the  intersection of cheyenne and commerce  was so intense some of the vehicles that  were hit were pushed into the empty lot  of the northeast corner of the  intersection north las vegas police  released photos of the vehicles involved  you can see how damaged they were many  of the vehicles were unrecognizable the  investigation markings are still on the  ground the intersection is now back open  but despite that the investigation into  this deadly crash is far from over as  loved ones grieve the loss of their  family time will hopefully provide more  answers into what happened  the investigation is 